<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Direct and Reported Speech</h1>
  <p class="topic-lead">Questions and tense choices</p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-lilac">
    <h2>Reported questions</h2>
    <p>Use <strong>asked if</strong> or <strong>asked whether</strong> for a yes/no question, then statement word order.</p>
    <p>“Are you coming?” asked John. → John asked <strong>if I was coming</strong>.</p>
    <p>Do not keep the question’s subject–verb inversion (<em>if was I coming</em>). The reported question normally ends with a full stop, not a question mark.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-mint">
    <h2>Backshift is common, not automatic</h2>
    <p>If the reporting verb is present, the tense usually stays the same. “He says, ‘I am hungry.’” → He says he <strong>is</strong> hungry.</p>
    <p>A speaker may also leave a statement in the present when it remains true: “The teacher said that water <strong>boils</strong> at 100°C.”</p>
    <p>Choose a tense that fits the reporting context and the meaning.</p>
  </section>
</div>
